NAME
       env - show the environment, or run a program with a changed one

SYNOPSIS
       env
       env [-i] [-u NAME] [NAME=VALUE...] COMMAND [ARGUMENT...]

DESCRIPTION
       Without arguments, env prints every environment variable, one
       NAME=value per line (like printenv). With a COMMAND it runs it with the
       NAME=VALUE settings added, and without the variables removed with -u.

       Scripts often start with #!/usr/bin/env bash so the program is found
       on the PATH.

OPTIONS
       -i     Start from an empty environment.

       -u NAME
              Remove NAME from the environment.

EXAMPLES
       Show variables whose name contains PATH:

           env | grep PATH

       Run one command with another language setting:

           env LANG=C date

SEE ALSO
       printenv(1), export(1), bash(1)
